{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.two_pow_ne_three_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.two_pow_ne_three_pow","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/VassilievMagnitudeA3.lean#L147-L154","doc":"The arithmetic core of `log₂ 3 ∉ ℚ`: `2^a` (`a ≥ 1`, even) never equals `3^b` (odd).\nHence `log₂ 3 = a/b` would force `2^a = 3^b`, impossible — so `r* ≈ log₂ 3` is a coincidence,\nnot a rational finite-type weight the substrate could produce. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.measured_milnor_weight_ne_rStar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.measured_milnor_weight_ne_rStar","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/VassilievMagnitudeA3.lean#L140-L143","doc":"The specific corpus-measured Milnor weight `−2 = J_Hopf(q=1)` is not `r*`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.no_integer_weight_eq_rStar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.no_integer_weight_eq_rStar","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/VassilievMagnitudeA3.lean#L129-L138","doc":"The length-A Milnor reading (`A−1=2`): the genuine μ̄(123) is realized as an INTEGER-valued\nVassiliev invariant (`BrunnianVassilievBridge.muBar_realized`, value `±1`), and the\ncorpus-measured Milnor ratio is the integer `−2`. No integer weight equals `r* ∈ (3/2, 2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.vassiliev_weight_cannot_supply_magnitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.vassiliev_weight_cannot_supply_magnitude","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/VassilievMagnitudeA3.lean#L117-L127","doc":"**MAIN (scope-(b) structural exclusion).** For every `h ≠ 0` the Vassiliev weight-to-Hecke\nratio `leadingWeight h / borrDeficit h ≤ 1 < 3/2 < r*`. A finite-type weight-system correction\nof the Borromean deficit cannot supply the `1.585×` A=3 magnitude factor: it is bounded above\nby the Hecke value (the full Markov-trace sum), whereas `r*` requires *exceeding* it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.rStar_lt_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.rStar_lt_two","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/VassilievMagnitudeA3.lean#L112-L113","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.rStar_gt_three_halves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.rStar_gt_three_halves","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/VassilievMagnitudeA3.lean#L109-L110","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.rStar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.rStar","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/VassilievMagnitudeA3.lean#L106-L107","doc":"The required A=3 magnitude factor `r* = μ₃ / c₃ ≈ 1.585`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.mu3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.mu3","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/VassilievMagnitudeA3.lean#L103-L104","doc":"Target additive-residual moment `μ₃ = +0.4708 MeV` (`AdditiveResidualSimplex`, #4320). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.c3bare","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.c3bare","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/VassilievMagnitudeA3.lean#L100-L101","doc":"Hecke-level near-miss `c₃ = +0.297 MeV` (#4364, the atom-dressed `H₉` Borromean lift). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.leadingWeight_le_borrDeficit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.leadingWeight_le_borrDeficit","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/VassilievMagnitudeA3.lean#L89-L96","doc":"**KEY (exact, all `h`).** The leading Vassiliev weight `(3/4)h⁴` is bounded ABOVE by the\nfull Borromean deficit `h⁴(3+h²)/(h²+4)`. Reason: `(3/4)(h²+4) = (3/4)h²+3 ≤ h²+3 = 3+h²`,\ni.e. the leading term is the smallest term of the positive convergent series. Consequently no\nfinite-type truncation exceeds the full (Hecke) value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.borrDeficit_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.borrDeficit_pos","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/VassilievMagnitudeA3.lean#L77-L85","doc":"For `h ≠ 0` the deficit is strictly positive (a positive-coefficient series). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.borrDeficit_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.borrDeficit_mul","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/VassilievMagnitudeA3.lean#L71-L75","doc":"Denominator is never zero (`h² + 4 > 0`); the deficit's defining polynomial identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.leadingWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.leadingWeight","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/VassilievMagnitudeA3.lean#L67-L69","doc":"The leading finite-type (Vassiliev degree `2(A−1)=4`) weight — the `h → 0` symbol of the\ndeficit: `(3+h²)/(h²+4) → 3/4`, so the leading weight is `(3/4)·h⁴`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.borrDeficit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.VassilievMagnitudeA3.borrDeficit","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/VassilievMagnitudeA3.lean#L63-L65","doc":"The proved A=3 Borromean 3-body deficit closed form `1 − τ_Borr(h)`, `h = q − q⁻¹`.\nThis is the finite-type object the Hecke Markov trace evaluates at `q₀`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}